Exercise: sa-software-review (chapter 13 lab)

Work on servera, with sudo or as root.

A local repository
 1. A repository in /srv/localrepo holding the packages zip and unzip,
    downloaded with dnf download --resolve, with metadata built by
    createrepo_c.
 2. /etc/yum.repos.d/local.repo for it: id localrepo, baseurl
    file:///srv/localrepo, enabled=1, gpgcheck=1 and the same gpgkey line
    as your distribution's repositories.
 3. zip (and its dependency unzip) installed using only that repository.

Other changes
 4. wget installed from the normal repositories.
 5. The package tree removed.
 6. The nginx module stream 1.24 enabled (do not install nginx).

On workstation
 7. Fill in answers.txt. Use rpm and ls on servera to find the answers.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-software-review
